1
00:00:00,192 --> 00:00:04,780
Third-rate graduate who can't find work in Japan. At night, she sleeps in internet cafes, numbing herself with alcohol.

2
00:00:04,980 --> 00:00:06,208
You know how bleak her nights are?

3
00:00:07,008 --> 00:00:11,080
At 8 in the evening, Yifu, 24 this year, has just finished another interview.

4
00:00:11,339 --> 00:00:16,320
She can't stay at school and hasn't rented a place. She spends every night at the internet cafe. Parole.

5
00:00:16,544 --> 00:00:20,928
It's the cheapest place to crash in the big city. Night here costs about 3,000 yen.

6
00:00:20,992 --> 00:00:26,751
It's definitely cheaper than a hotel. The key is, Japanese internet cafes have private booths lined with sofas.

7
00:00:26,783 --> 00:00:30,911
If you want to sleep, it's no problem. and your personal safety is guaranteed.

8
00:00:31,071 --> 00:00:34,975
How would a young woman like Yifu dare spend the night in a place like this?

9
00:00:35,584 --> 00:00:40,259
Once inside, she hasn't had dinner yet, so she turns on the computer to order food. It's one of the cafe's main features.

10
00:00:40,500 --> 00:00:45,600
They offer all kinds of food. No matter when you get hungry, just a few clicks and the staff will bring it right to you.

11
00:00:46,304 --> 00:00:49,299
Of course, this convenience comes at a price. The food here is expensive.

12
00:00:49,659 --> 00:00:52,320
Even a simple bowl of noodles or rice costs 30 to 40 yen.

13
00:00:52,351 --> 00:00:55,712
But Yifu doesn't eat here every day. She only treats herself on Fridays.

14
00:00:56,095 --> 00:01:00,768
Waiting for her food, she reviews her resume, looking for ways to improve it.

15
00:01:00,832 --> 00:01:05,632
She's been job hunting for a while now, but still hasn't found anything, so Yifu is pretty frustrated.

16
00:01:05,695 --> 00:01:08,420
To relieve the stress, she often uses alcohol to numb herself.

17
00:01:08,659 --> 00:01:12,287
A moment ago, Yifu looked downcast, but now with a beer, her eyes light up.

18
00:01:12,799 --> 00:01:18,560
She takes a couple of big gulps. It's pure bliss. A few of today's worries seem to disappear with each sip of beer.

19
00:01:19,007 --> 00:01:21,439
Look at her face. You can see how much it relaxes her.

20
00:01:21,504 --> 00:01:27,060
Soon enough, her food arrives at the door. Yifu ordered a noodle box meal. I wouldn't guess someone so petite could eat so much.

21
00:01:27,359 --> 00:01:32,000
How did things come to this point? It's really her own doing. Her grades were never good.

22
00:01:32,379 --> 00:01:35,900
So after high school, she went to a vocational school, unlike regular universities.

23
00:01:36,180 --> 00:01:41,959
These are skill-based schools focused on getting you a job. Yifu studied art, which is kind of like our field skill set.

24
00:01:42,120 --> 00:01:46,719
Even though the job prospects aren't bad, he just never liked studying. He just drifts through each day.

25
00:01:47,379 --> 00:01:53,152
For two years, all he has is a diploma. He hasn't learned much. Sometimes, Yifu really regrets it.

26
00:01:53,504 --> 00:01:58,200
After all, to survive in society, you need both education and skills. Now he's on his own in Tokyo.

27
00:01:58,719 --> 00:02:04,543
No background, no connections. No wonder he keeps hitting walls job hunting. Every time he's told to go home and wait.

28
00:02:04,992 --> 00:02:09,759
Yifu feels helpless. After eating his fill, just plans to crash in bed after a long day.

29
00:02:09,824 --> 00:02:13,219
Though he's exhausted and sleepy, Yifu still tosses and turns, unable to sleep.

30
00:02:13,400 --> 00:02:18,800
Of course, he hasn't found a job yet, and he's almost out of money. Soon he might not even afford the internet cafe.

31
00:02:19,080 --> 00:02:20,659
The more he tries to sleep, the more anxious he gets.

32
00:02:20,879 --> 00:02:23,780
So he gets up to take a walk. He lives in an internet cafe. He doesn't have much luck.

33
00:02:23,860 --> 00:02:27,487
He often runs out of clean clothes, so sometimes he just skips showers.

34
00:02:27,616 --> 00:02:33,500
After two or three days, he doesn't really smell, and no one notices. He figures he can put up with it. Heading out, he buys another can of beer.

35
00:02:33,620 --> 00:02:35,800
He plans to drink and wander around to ease his mind.

36
00:02:35,879 --> 00:02:40,360
In his situation, Yifu admits there's not much else he can do. All he can do is keep job hunting.

37
00:02:40,520 --> 00:02:46,439
If he really can't find anything, he'll make a backup plan. After all, he has to work eventually. He can't live off his parents forever.

38
00:02:47,020 --> 00:02:52,360
But Yifu honestly doesn't know what he's good at. He's completely lost right now. That's how it is for most young people these days

39
00:02:52,520 --> 00:02:56,319
No direction, no confidence All she can do now is get herself together

40
00:02:56,599 --> 00:03:02,431
She hopes to find a job before her money runs out It's already one in the morning Ifu finally returns to the internet cafe to sleep

41
00:03:02,719 --> 00:03:04,639
For her, tonight might be another sleepless night

